Defect: SMI-INVALID-DATE https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-invalid-date

LAST-UPDATED is an empty string, and the MODULE-IDENTITY has no REVISION
to take a date from. The only date the file carries is the MIB builder's
own stamp in its opening comment, Wednesday, April 20, 2016 at 17:07:15,
so the repair is that minute. It is the date the file was generated,
which is the nearest thing to a last update the text records, and not a
date the vendor wrote into the clause.

No publisher on record serves this module, so the baseline is the text
this repository carried before the repair; which publication that was is
not recovered.

--- a/SLE-EPON-MIB
+++ b/SLE-EPON-MIB
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 	
 	
 		sleEpon MODULE-IDENTITY 
-			LAST-UPDATED ""		-- 
+			LAST-UPDATED "201604201707Z"		-- 
 			ORGANIZATION 
 				"Organization."
 			CONTACT-INFO 
